  "Title": "Motif Enrichment Analysis of Regulatory DNA Sequences",
  "Version": "0.99.5",
  "Encoding": "UTF-8",
  "biocViews": "SequenceMatching, Transcription, GeneRegulation,\nMotifAnnotation",
  "Authors@R": "c(person(\"Federico\", \"Zambelli\", email = \"federico.zambelli@unimi.it\", \nrole = c(\"aut\", \"cre\"), comment = c(ORCID = \"0000-0003-3487-4331\")),\nperson(\"Giulio\", \"Pavesi\", email = \"giulio.pavesi@unimi.it\", role = \"aut\",\ncomment = c(ORCID = \"0000-0001-5705-6249\")),\nperson(\"Diana\", \"Betelli\", role = \"ctb\"),\nperson(\"Italy's National Recovery and Resilience Plan (PNRR)\",\nrole = \"fnd\", comment = \"project ELIXIRNextGenIT, R0000010\"))",
  "Description": "R implementation of the 'Pscan' algorithm for motif\nenrichment analysis in regulatory DNA sequences, based on\nZambelli et al. (2009) <doi:10.1093/nar/gkp464>. 'PscanR' scans\na set of DNA sequences (e.g., promoters) from co-regulated or\nco-expressed genes, using transcription factor binding motifs\nfrom databases such as JASPAR. It identifies significantly\nenriched motifs, providing thus hints on which transcription\nfactors could be common regulators of the genes studied,\ntogether with the location of their candidate binding sites in\nthe sequences.",
